# Cursor Rules for BC250-WinDv Repository
# Hardware Target: AMD BC-250 APU (1002:13FE rev 00, Cyan Skillfish 2 / GC 10.1.3)
# OS Target: Windows 11 x64 (Kernel Mode KMDF + full WDDM Display+Render miniport)
# Last revision: 2026-09-02
# Normative core is IDENTICAL to CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and GEMINI.md. Change all four together.

---

## 0. Goal, and the single source of truth

GOAL: run games on Windows 11 on the BC-250 — 24 CUs, 16 GB GDDR6, monitor on the board's
own DisplayPort, via D3D12/Vulkan, with NO WARP and NO software fallback.

SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH: `BASE_DE_AVANCO.md`
  - Table 1 = what is already validated on silicon (45 items, archived proof).
  - Table 2 = what is missing, ordered by priority P1..P9, WITH THE TEST THAT CLOSES EACH ITEM.
ROADMAP: `docs/164_ROADMAP_WDDM_JOGOS.md`
NORMATIVE RULES / CONFIDENCE VOCABULARY: `rules.md`

CURRENT ARCHITECTURE: display v1 is INHERITED from the UEFI GOP — single-mode VidPn,
scanout allocation in real VRAM, `DxgkDdiPresent` in BLT model via SDMA, VSync READ from
the OTG frame counter. DCN is NOT on the critical path. Writing to any DCN register is
FORBIDDEN outside priority P9; reading is allowed.

WHERE WE ACTUALLY ARE: the WDDM adapter has NEVER reached Code 0. `dxgkrnl` rejects the
device on return from `StartDevice`, 5 s after bind, without ever asking for `DRIVERCAPS`
(items 97 and 102). Direct compute and the KMDOD/GOP display ARE proven on silicon.
Nothing of WDDM render is.

CLOSED PATHS — do not reopen: render-only under `Class=Display` (failed, `docs/162`);
`MiscCaps.ComputeOnly` (unreachable); cross-adapter / MCDM as the destination (single-die APU).

